{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998452-so-game-mechanics-question-throwing-a-torch-at-someone-versus-swinging-a-torch","id":998452,"title":"So game mechanics question: throwing a torch at someone versus swinging a torch","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-04T15:00:29-07:00","id":998452,"title":"So game mechanics question: throwing a torch at someone versus swinging a torch","content":"So I had a question about dice pools. I'm the ST and was able to just run with something else but I wanted to find out how the game mechanics actually handled this. <br /> <br /> So it is my understanding throwing a weapon is Strength + Athletics - Defense and swinging a weapon is Strength + Weaponry - Defense. <br /> <br /> We're playing Chronicles of Darkness as a prologue to a mage the awakening game. <br /> <br /> The PCs are high schoolers who are rescuing their friend from an other worldly labyrinth in a haunted house. Actually an abyssal corrupted Demesne that was created by a now dead cabal of Mysterium mages murdered by the campaign's main villain. No one fixed this because in the universe I created the five orders are extinct in the region the game takes place in and when they awaken, no one is going to be there to tell them what they should and shouldn't do. But the PCs don't know any of this yet. The house is bigger on the inside than it is on the outside and there was a mysterious door that led to an infinite maze they had to learn to navigate using symbology. <br /> <br /> Oh and of course there were monsters, inspired by Silent Hill.Creatures of sick and twisted nightmare, spawn of the abyss, manifested while in the maze because twilight isn't a thing in the maze. One of the PCs dubbed the trashier and trashier corridors and libraries and bedrooms, coiling and increasingly alien as they went deeper &quot;Shit Narnia.&quot; They fought their way through, discovering that the creatures were vulnerable to fire. They were able to reach the menagerie where their friend was caged and defeat the boss with some nice ingenuity, will power, and coming up with an insane plan built on conjecture that I decided was true. They manage to pick up a mysterious book while they were there, written in a mysterious language they are just beginning to be able to interpret: the last copy of the corpus mysteriorum, a priceless artifact which they can't read but the party psychic is eager to attempt to study anyway, given to them by a mage ghost who wasn't forthright with answers but gave them hooks a plenty for future adventures and also their eventual awakenings. <br /> <br /> We ran into something strange with the mechanics during the fight. None of the players had put any points into weaponry or firearms but one of them was a football player and had put 5 points in athletics. Since the dice pool. for throwing something was so high and swinging the torch was so low, it begged a question of it was that hitting a grappled monster was a chance roll but throwing the torch at it could get exceptional successes. &quot;Can't I just walk up an drop the torch on him instead of swinging it?&quot; was the question I wasn't sure how to answer. I concocted some bullshit to get us through and was going to ask you fine folks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1563-oriontyson","name":"OrionTyson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T15:14:10-07:00","id":998464,"title":"","content":"Walking up and dropping it wouldn't constitute a throw, wouldn't make use of the character's skill as an athlete, and wouldn't provide enough force to really deal health levels of damage. But, there's no reason you can't make a thrown weapon attack against a grappled target. As per the rules for throwing objects, you do need Strength equal to or greater than the object's size to throw it, and I would probably slap an improvised weapon penalty on the attack roll if the object isn't made to be used as a thrown weapon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T15:44:39-07:00","id":998475,"title":"","content":"Seconding Charly.<br /> <br /> I would also say that it being torch wouldn't really do anything special when thrown. Depending on what the torch is made of you may as well be throwing a stick. Getting the flames to do any damage would be impossible, and embers would be negligible (except with a called shot to the eyes).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T16:43:35-07:00","id":998499,"title":"","content":"ah well, we did it wrong. We're still learning the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1563-oriontyson","name":"OrionTyson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T17:51:56-07:00","id":998524,"title":"","content":"There's always room for interpretation. While I agree that normally such a roll should be made how Charlaquinn described it, if there's a narrative reason why another dice pool could be used, then I say you should have the option (well, with the GM's approval). While the rules should be adhered to for consistency, sticking too close to them doesn't make for a very fun experience. Plus, as someone who has had to GM on the spot with a bit of tension and not having enough time to check the rules, concocting bullshit to keep things going is definitely a legitimate strategy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T18:55:51-07:00","id":998550,"title":"","content":"Oh, yeah, I think you made the right call by making a ruling in the moment. The important thing is you made a decision instead of letting it slow you down. Just letting you know the RAW since you asked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T01:11:12-07:00","id":998647,"title":"","content":"I would simply let athlete to throw torch like spear in to grapple - roll <b>Dexterity + Athletics - Target's Defense</b>, Torch does 1L damage, as it's fires rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T16:30:52-07:00","id":998939,"title":"","content":"Makes sense. I had it do aggs because of the particular abyssal horror's physiology. They had bodies that were as cold as dry ice but had a skin texture like paper. I also wanted to give the otherwise mortal / sleepwalker PCs some kind of chance to kill them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1563-oriontyson","name":"OrionTyson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T20:01:25-07:00","id":999016,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I have no answer to your mechanical question, but &quot;Shit Narnia&quot; sounds like a reference to John Dies at the End.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T21:36:21-07:00","id":999061,"title":"","content":"Not an answer to the actual question but I could see in the case of trying to strike an opponent successfully grappled by an ally treating it has a teamwork action, with the grappler rolling an extra action to give bonus dice to the actor on the grounds that he is actively opening the target up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T03:50:12-08:00","id":1000204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998452-so-game-mechanics-question-throwing-a-torch-at-someone-versus-swinging-a-torch?p=999016#post999016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I have no answer to your mechanical question, but &quot;Shit Narnia&quot; sounds like a reference to John Dies at the End.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, yes it is.It was one of my players who called it that. It didn't have a name, neither did the monsters. It was an abyssal verge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1563-oriontyson","name":"OrionTyson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T04:10:19-08:00","id":1000210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OrionTyson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/998452-so-game-mechanics-question-throwing-a-torch-at-someone-versus-swinging-a-torch?p=1000204#post1000204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes, yes it is.It was one of my players who called it that. It didn't have a name, neither did the monsters. It was an abyssal verge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, definite coolness points for the reference. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T15:57:25-08:00","id":1001530,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I noticed that throwing stuff at people is good, and after some meditation, I arrived at conclusion that it's a good, genre-reinforcing thing. Athletics is a great skill to have for the genre in general. Notice how hard sometimes is to believably work-in Weaponry/Brawl/other combat skill into a &quot;normal&quot; character, while Athletics is very easy to insert without drastically changing the character? Yeah. Athletics is a good solution for a genre-related problem where characters that don't have previous experience and combat related training probably WILL be put in combat related life threatening situations. So Athletics was given combat-related perks that help these characters survive and emulate the genre; Athletics gives you defense needed to survive and ability to actively overcome problems. Monster trying to catch you? Maybe try climbing or jumping. Need to slow it down?<br /> <br /> Well, what characters in horrors do when they need to slow down a pursuer? They drop a bookshelf on them, they start throwing chairs and stuff! And Athletics helps you with that. So basically, throwing being easily accessible and relatively effective strategy is a feature.<br /> Note that it isn't a perfect strategy, though; it has very real issues. Most of improvised objects for thrown weapons will be relatively low quality and low stats, and you won't have access to many benefits that come from using equipment in it's intended way. While on paper Athletics-kiting might sound too good for non-combatant characters, actual practice will usually show that unless you really twink for it (like, professional knife throwing ninja with 40 knives on you), it will usually be just fine. <br /> So yeah, 5 points of athletics is a lot. Encourage your player to figure out how to put it in work, because Athletics-based solutions to combat problems can be really fun; instead of shooting the monster, drop something heavy on it, throw a chair, basically, be a movie hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}